course: dictionary
lesson: 3685
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer wants. The word «flaming» is a good example. Read the clues before you choose a meaning.
explain: «The flaming bus is late again!» Nothing is on fire here. In British, Irish and Australian talk, flaming is a mild swear word, a softer stand-in for «bloody», used to show annoyance. It is old-fashioned and can sound funny, so do not use it at school.
explain: «A flaming torch» means a torch that is burning with flames. «Flaming red hair» means bright red or orange, like fire. The clues tell you which meaning fits: is anything burning, or is someone just cross?
fact: Flaming can be an adjective, an adverb or a verb form: flame, flames, flamed, flaming.
fact: As a mild swear word, «flaming» means annoying or cross, as in «that flaming dog»; it is mainly used in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: «Flaming» can mean burning with flames, as in «a flaming torch».
fact: «Flaming» can mean bright red or orange, like fire, as in «flaming red hair».
fact: Online, to flame someone means to send angry, insulting messages, so always be kind when you type.
exercise: «The flaming bus is late again!» Is anything on fire? | Yes, the bus is full of flames | Yes, the bus is burning | *No, flaming here is a stand-in for a swear word
exercise: «The villagers carried a flaming torch through the dark wood.» What does flaming mean here? | Sending rude messages | Bright red like a sunset | Very angry | *Burning with flames
exercise: «Her hair was flaming red in the sunshine.» What does flaming mean here? | Burning with flames | A mild swear word | Very angry | *Bright red or orange, like fire
test: Read «a flaming row». What does flaming mean here? | *Very angry or violent | Sending messages online | Bright red like fire | Burning with flames
test: Jess sent a nasty message to her friend, and her teacher says she was flaming her. What does flaming mean? | Feeling very tired | Cooking food on a grill | Glowing softly in the dark | *Sending angry, insulting messages online
exam: Ben shouts, «That flaming dog has eaten my sandwich!» What does flaming show about Ben's feelings? | Ben is very happy | Ben is on fire | *Annoyance, as a mild swear word | The dog is bright red
